{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XGLovaP9DEnwgBwMZ3HkWj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers\n2\t\n3\tPre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation using an adaptive size threshold, rather than pre-allocating for the maximum AIR size. The previous pre-allocation attempt (prealloc-round0-buffers) failed because it pre-allocated for the largest AIR's intermediates (~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB), causing systemic GPU memory pressure that degraded all phases. The adaptive approach pre-allocates buffers sized for the Nth-percentile AIR (e.g., 95th percentile), covering 95%+ of AIRs while keeping total allocation manageable. Small/medium AIRs (the vast majority at APC 300) skip the global MEMORY_MANAGER mutex entirely, while the few large AIRs fall back to dynamic allocation. This addresses the same root cause as the successful GKR pre-alloc optimization (which saved 217ms): eliminating per-AIR mutex contention and cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync serialization across 8 concurrent worker threads.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7b52780-6e9b-4892-943d-0d0679c1a1bd","uuid":"64dc0f4a-df89-42b7-96bf-e05b71b73a93","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:23:31.428Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers\n\nPre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation using an adaptive size threshold, rather than pre-allocating for the maximum AIR size. The previous pre-allocation attempt (prealloc-round0-buffers) failed because it pre-allocated for the largest AIR's intermediates (~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB), causing systemic GPU memory pressure that degraded all phases. The adaptive approach pre-allocates buffers sized for the Nth-percentile AIR (e.g., 95th percentile), covering 95%+ of AIRs while keeping total allocation manageable. Small/medium AIRs (the vast majority at APC 300) skip the global MEMORY_MANAGER mutex entirely, while the few large AIRs fall back to dynamic allocation. This addresses the same root cause as the successful GKR pre-alloc optimization (which saved 217ms): eliminating per-AIR mutex contention and cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync serialization across 8 concurrent worker threads.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
