{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017oUbC93JrZZe1uWEQCKh6s","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 buffers with adaptive size threshold\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR GPU memory allocation overhead in the Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread buffer pools, following the pattern that saved 217ms in GKR input evaluation (`prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`). Use an adaptive size threshold to avoid the GPU memory pressure that caused the previous Round 0 pre-allocation attempt (`prealloc-round0-buffers`) to fail.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Round 0 orchestration\n10\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n11\t\n12\t`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` processes 623 AIRs (at APC 300) across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Work items are sorted by descending height and distributed round-robin.\n13\t\n14\tEach thread calls `process_air_round0` (mod.rs:140-272) per AIR, which calls two evaluation functions sequentially:\n15\t\n16\t### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n17\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n18\t\n19\tAllocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions + 3 frees = 6 total):\n20\t1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n21\t2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n22\t3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)\n23\t\n24\tAll three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`).\n25\t\n26\tThe zerocheck `buffer_size` comes from `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size` (round0.rs:51-53), which is pre-computed in the proving key and available during Phase 1 work item preparation.\n27\t\n28\t### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n29\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`\n30\t\n31\tAllocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions + 6 frees = 12 total):\n32\t1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n33\t2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n34\t3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)\n35\t4. `d_rules` — from `encoded_rules.to_device()` (line 210)\n36\t5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)\n37\t6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)\n38\t\n39\tItems 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (weights depend on runtime `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows`; rules depend on a DAG built per-AIR). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.\n40\t\n41\t**Critical note:** The logup `buffer_size` (round0.rs:212) is **not** available from `pk.other_data` — it comes from a `SymbolicRulesGpu` constructed dynamically inside the function (round0.rs:161-206) via `SymbolicDagBuilder` + `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`. This DAG is deterministic per AIR but is NOT pre-computed in `AirDataGpu`. This must be addressed (see Step 1).\n42\t\n43\t### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`\n44\t- `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements\n45\t\n46\t### Total allocation overhead\n47\tPer AIR: ~6 mutex acquisitions for the 3 pre-allocatable buffers in each of the 2 functions (intermediates + temp_sums + result = 3 alloc+free pairs × 2 functions = 12 mutex acquisitions). Plus ~8 more for items 4-6, d_main_parts, and their frees. Total: **~20 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.\n48\t\n49\tWith 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~24,920 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads.\n50\t\n51\t### Why this is slow\n52\tThe global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~20 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.\n53\t\n54\t### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed\n55\tThe `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms).\n56\t\n57\t## Changes\n58\t\n59\t### Step 1: Add `logup_round0_buffer_size` to `AirDataGpu`\n60\t\n61\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n62\t\n63\tAdd a new field to `AirDataGpu` (line 24-32):\n64\t```rust\n65\tpub struct AirDataGpu {\n66\t    pub interaction_rules: InteractionEvalRules,\n67\t    pub zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>,\n68\t    pub zerocheck_mle: ConstraintOnlyRules<false>,\n69\t    pub zerocheck_monomials: Option<ZerocheckMonomials>,\n70\t    pub interaction_monomials: Option<InteractionMonomials>,\n71\t    /// Buffer size for the logup round0 interaction evaluation DAG.\n72\t    /// Computed at keygen time to allow pre-computation of buffer sizes\n73\t    /// during Round 0 work item preparation.\n74\t    pub logup_round0_buffer_size: u32,\n75\t}\n76\t```\n77\t\n78\tIn `AirDataGpu::new` (pkey.rs:86-114), compute this using the same logic currently in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (round0.rs:161-211):\n79\t1. Create `SymbolicDagBuilder`, add interaction count/message expressions\n80\t2. Sort+dedup constraint indices\n81\t3. Build `SymbolicExpressionDag`, then `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`\n82\t4. Store `rules.buffer_size` as `logup_round0_buffer_size`\n83\t\n84\tThis makes the logup `buffer_size` available from `pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` during Phase 1.\n85\t\n86\t### Step 2: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n87\t\n88\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n89\t\n90\t```rust\n91\tpub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n92\t    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)\n93\t    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n94\t    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for zerocheck\n95\t    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n96\t    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for zerocheck (data copied to host before reuse)\n97\t    pub zc_sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n98\t    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for logup\n99\t    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n100\t    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for logup\n101\t    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n102\t    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup\n103\t    pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n104\t}\n105\t```\n106\t\n107\tNo separate capacity tracking fields — the pre-allocated `DeviceBuffer.len()` IS the capacity. The caller compares the AIR's required size against `buf.len()` to decide whether to use the pre-allocated buffer.\n108\t\n109\t### Step 3: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`\n110\t\n111\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n112\t\n113\tAdd pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct:\n114\t\n115\t```rust\n116\tstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n117\t    // ... existing fields ...\n118\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates capacity needed\n119\t    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n120\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed\n121\t    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n122\t    /// num_cosets_zc * skip_domain (zerocheck result size)\n123\t    zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n124\t    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed (uses logup_round0_buffer_size from Step 1)\n125\t    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n126\t    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed\n127\t    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n128\t    /// num_cosets_logup * skip_domain (logup result size)\n129\t    logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n130\t}\n131\t```\n132\t\n133\tCompute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926):\n134\t- `local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree`\n135\t- `skip_domain = 1 << l_skip`\n136\t- `num_x = 1 << n_lift` where `n_lift = n.max(0) as usize`\n137\t- `num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1)` (mod.rs:166)\n138\t- `num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg` (mod.rs:213)\n139\t- Zerocheck `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size`\n140\t- Logup `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` (from Step 1)\n141\t- Call `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc, max_temp_bytes)` and the other 5 FFI size functions to get actual sizes.\n142\t\n143\t### Step 4: Compute threshold and pre-allocate\n144\t\n145\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)\n146\t\n147\tAfter building work items with their buffer sizes:\n148\t\n149\t1. For each of the 6 buffer types, find the maximum across ALL work items.\n150\t2. If the maximum for any buffer type is 0 (e.g., all AIRs have no zerocheck constraints), use capacity 1 as a sentinel (DeviceBuffer panics on size 0). Track this so the fallback path is used for those buffers.\n151\t3. Compute total per-thread bytes from the 6 max values.\n152\t4. Memory budget: `per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)`.\n153\t5. If total per-thread bytes > per_thread_budget: reduce `num_threads` until it fits, same pattern as GKR (gkr_input.rs:296-303).\n154\t6. If after reducing to `num_threads=1` it still exceeds 2GB: skip pre-allocation entirely and use the current dynamic path.\n155\t7. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of `Round0ThreadBuffers`.\n156\t\n157\t### Step 5: Modify evaluation functions to accept pre-allocated buffers\n158\t\n159\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n160\t\n161\t#### D2H copy handling (addresses review finding 1)\n162\t\n163\t`DeviceBuffer` does not distinguish capacity from logical length — `len()` returns the allocation size. `to_host_on_current_stream()` copies `len()` elements. When a pre-allocated buffer has capacity larger than the actual output, the D2H copy would transfer excess data.\n164\t\n165\t**Solution:** Create a correctly-sized `DeviceBuffer` view using `ManuallyDrop` for D2H copies:\n166\t\n167\t```rust\n168\tuse std::mem::ManuallyDrop;\n169\t\n170\t/// Create a non-owning DeviceBuffer view with the correct logical length for D2H copies.\n171\t/// SAFETY: `buf` must have capacity >= `len`, and the caller must ensure `buf` outlives the view.\n172\tunsafe fn device_view<T>(buf: &DeviceBuffer<T>, len: usize) -> ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer<T>> {\n173\t    ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(buf.as_mut_ptr(), len))\n174\t}\n175\t```\n176\t\n177\tThis creates a `DeviceBuffer` that points to the same GPU memory but has the correct `len` for D2H copies. `ManuallyDrop` prevents the Drop impl from freeing the pre-allocated memory.\n178\t\n179\t#### `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` changes\n180\t\n181\tAdd parameter:\n182\t```rust\n183\tprealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>,\n184\t// (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals)\n185\t```\n186\t\n187\tReplace allocation of `intermediates` (lines 63-68):\n188\t```rust\n189\tlet (mut intermediates, owns_intermediates) = if let Some((ref mut pre_inter, _, _)) = prealloc {\n190\t    if intermed_capacity > 0 && pre_inter.len() >= intermed_capacity {\n191\t        // Reuse pre-allocated buffer (no mutex, no alloc)\n192\t        // SAFETY: pre_inter has capacity >= intermed_capacity\n193\t        (unsafe { ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(pre_inter.as_mut_ptr(), intermed_capacity)) }, false)\n194\t    } else {\n195\t        (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity.max(1))), true)\n196\t    }\n197\t} else if intermed_capacity > 0 {\n198\t    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)), true)\n199\t} else {\n200\t    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::new()), false)\n201\t};\n202\t```\n203\t\n204\tApply the same pattern for `temp_sums_buffer` and `sp_evals`.\n205\t\n206\tFor the D2H copy of `sp_evals` in the caller (`process_air_round0`, mod.rs:184):\n207\t```rust\n208\tlet actual_len = w.zc_sp_evals_cap;\n209\tlet view = unsafe { device_view(&bufs.zc_sp_evals, actual_len) };\n210\tlet q_evals = view.to_host_on_current_stream()?;\n211\t```\n212\t\n213\tAt function end: if `owns_intermediates`, explicitly drop (frees via mutex). If not, ManuallyDrop prevents freeing.\n214\t\n215\t#### `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` changes\n216\t\n217\tSame pattern. Add `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).\n218\t\n219\tItems 4-6 (`d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`) remain dynamically allocated. These 3 alloc+free pairs per logup call still go through the mutex. This is unavoidable since their data is AIR-specific and runtime-dependent.\n220\t\n221\t### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers\n222\t\n223\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n224\t\n225\tChange signature:\n226\t```rust\n227\tfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n228\t    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n229\t    bufs: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n230\t) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError>\n231\t```\n232\t\n233\tInside the function:\n234\t1. Check if zerocheck buffers fit:\n235\t   ```rust\n236\t   let zc_prealloc = if w.zc_intermed_cap <= bufs.zc_intermediates.len()\n237\t       && w.zc_temp_sums_cap <= bufs.zc_temp_sums.len()\n238\t       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap <= bufs.zc_sp_evals.len()\n239\t       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap > 0\n240\t   {\n241\t       Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))\n242\t   } else {\n243\t       None\n244\t   };\n245\t   ```\n246\t2. Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(..., zc_prealloc)`.\n247\t3. For the D2H copy: if pre-allocated was used, create a `device_view` with the actual output length (`w.zc_sp_evals_cap`). If dynamic allocation was used, the buffer already has the correct length.\n248\t4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()`, the host data is in a `Vec<EF>`. The pre-allocated GPU buffer is safe to reuse for the next AIR.\n249\t5. Same pattern for logup buffers, using `bufs.logup_*`.\n250\t\n251\t### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn\n252\t\n253\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (Phase 2, lines 963-985)\n254\t\n255\tPass one `Round0ThreadBuffers` to each spawned thread:\n256\t```rust\n257\tlet handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n258\t    .into_iter()\n259\t    .zip(thread_items.into_iter())\n260\t    .enumerate()\n261\t    .map(|(thread_id, (mut bufs, indices))| {\n262\t        let items = &work_items;\n263\t        s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n264\t            let t0 = std::time::Instant::now();\n265\t            let results: Vec<_> = indices\n266\t                .iter()\n267\t                .map(|&idx| process_air_round0(&items[idx], &mut bufs))\n268\t                .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n269\t            tracing::debug!(thread_id, elapsed_ms = t0.elapsed().as_millis(), num_airs = indices.len(), \"round0 thread done\");\n270\t            Ok(results)\n271\t        })\n272\t    })\n273\t    .collect();\n274\t```\n275\t\n276\tFor the single-thread path (`num_threads <= 1`), pass the single buffer set similarly.\n277\t\n278\t## Invariants\n279\t\n280\t1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.\n281\t2. **D2H copy correctness**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) use `ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(ptr, actual_len)>` views for D2H copies, ensuring exactly the correct number of elements are transferred to host. No excess data is copied.\n282\t3. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function calls `current_stream_sync()` (copy.rs:147), ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete before reuse.\n283\t4. **ManuallyDrop safety**: Views created via `ManuallyDrop` never free GPU memory. Only the owning `Round0ThreadBuffers` (dropped after all threads complete) frees the pre-allocated memory.\n284\t5. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively.\n285\t6. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. If it still exceeds after `num_threads=1`, pre-allocation is skipped entirely.\n286\t7. **APC 0 behavior**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`. If the single AIR's buffers exceed pre-allocated capacity, the fallback path is used.\n287\t8. **Kernel buffer semantics**: Intermediates and temp_sums are scratch space — kernels write to them but the data is never read back to host. Using a pre-allocated buffer with capacity > required is harmless; the kernel indexes only up to `intermed_capacity`, not the buffer's allocated length.\n288\t\n289\t## Measurement Plan\n290\t\n291\t### Commands\n292\t```bash\n293\t# In powdr repo:\n294\tcd results/pairing\n295\tPROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n296\t\n297\t# Build\n298\tcargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n299\t\n300\t# Before measurements (3 runs for APC 300)\n301\tfor i in 1 2 3; do\n302\t  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion\n303\tdone\n304\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n305\t\n306\t# After implementing the optimization, rebuild and re-measure:\n307\tfor i in 1 2 3; do\n308\t  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion\n309\tdone\n310\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n311\t\n312\tpython3 ~/spec.py after_apc300_1/metrics.json after_apc300\n313\t```\n314\t\n315\t### Expected results\n316\t- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-240ms (13-28% improvement)\n317\t- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1385ms (3-5% improvement)\n318\t- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs)\n319\t- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise\n320\t\n321\t### Stability verification\n322\tCompare medians of 3 before-runs vs 3 after-runs for APC 300 to confirm improvement exceeds noise (~20ms).\n323\t\n324\t### Nsight validation\n325\tRun nsight on APC 300 and verify:\n326\t- Fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync API calls in the Round 0 NVTX span\n327\t- Reduced mutex contention visible in CPU thread timeline (fewer blocked intervals)\n328\t\n329\t## Rollback Criteria\n330\t\n331\t1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs). Below the noise floor.\n332\t2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms**. Any single-phase regression (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) > 30ms.\n333\t3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. Fallback path must not add overhead.\n334\t4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed).\n335\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7b52780-6e9b-4892-943d-0d0679c1a1bd","uuid":"ca227d71-cf72-49d3-a9f8-9abf57a76c31","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:23:34.820Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 buffers with adaptive size threshold\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR GPU memory allocation overhead in the Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread buffer pools, following the pattern that saved 217ms in GKR input evaluation (`prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`). Use an adaptive size threshold to avoid the GPU memory pressure that caused the previous Round 0 pre-allocation attempt (`prealloc-round0-buffers`) to fail.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Round 0 orchestration\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n\n`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` processes 623 AIRs (at APC 300) across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Work items are sorted by descending height and distributed round-robin.\n\nEach thread calls `process_air_round0` (mod.rs:140-272) per AIR, which calls two evaluation functions sequentially:\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n\nAllocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions + 3 frees = 6 total):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)\n\nAll three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`).\n\nThe zerocheck `buffer_size` comes from `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size` (round0.rs:51-53), which is pre-computed in the proving key and available during Phase 1 work item preparation.\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`\n\nAllocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions + 6 frees = 12 total):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)\n4. `d_rules` — from `encoded_rules.to_device()` (line 210)\n5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)\n6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)\n\nItems 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (weights depend on runtime `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows`; rules depend on a DAG built per-AIR). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.\n\n**Critical note:** The logup `buffer_size` (round0.rs:212) is **not** available from `pk.other_data` — it comes from a `SymbolicRulesGpu` constructed dynamically inside the function (round0.rs:161-206) via `SymbolicDagBuilder` + `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`. This DAG is deterministic per AIR but is NOT pre-computed in `AirDataGpu`. This must be addressed (see Step 1).\n\n### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`\n- `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements\n\n### Total allocation overhead\nPer AIR: ~6 mutex acquisitions for the 3 pre-allocatable buffers in each of the 2 functions (intermediates + temp_sums + result = 3 alloc+free pairs × 2 functions = 12 mutex acquisitions). Plus ~8 more for items 4-6, d_main_parts, and their frees. Total: **~20 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.\n\nWith 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~24,920 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads.\n\n### Why this is slow\nThe global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~20 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.\n\n### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed\nThe `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms).\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Add `logup_round0_buffer_size` to `AirDataGpu`\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n\nAdd a new field to `AirDataGpu` (line 24-32):\n```rust\npub struct AirDataGpu {\n    pub interaction_rules: InteractionEvalRules,\n    pub zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>,\n    pub zerocheck_mle: ConstraintOnlyRules<false>,\n    pub zerocheck_monomials: Option<ZerocheckMonomials>,\n    pub interaction_monomials: Option<InteractionMonomials>,\n    /// Buffer size for the logup round0 interaction evaluation DAG.\n    /// Computed at keygen time to allow pre-computation of buffer sizes\n    /// during Round 0 work item preparation.\n    pub logup_round0_buffer_size: u32,\n}\n```\n\nIn `AirDataGpu::new` (pkey.rs:86-114), compute this using the same logic currently in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (round0.rs:161-211):\n1. Create `SymbolicDagBuilder`, add interaction count/message expressions\n2. Sort+dedup constraint indices\n3. Build `SymbolicExpressionDag`, then `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`\n4. Store `rules.buffer_size` as `logup_round0_buffer_size`\n\nThis makes the logup `buffer_size` available from `pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` during Phase 1.\n\n### Step 2: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)\n    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for zerocheck\n    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for zerocheck (data copied to host before reuse)\n    pub zc_sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for logup\n    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for logup\n    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup\n    pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n}\n```\n\nNo separate capacity tracking fields — the pre-allocated `DeviceBuffer.len()` IS the capacity. The caller compares the AIR's required size against `buf.len()` to decide whether to use the pre-allocated buffer.\n\n### Step 3: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct:\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    // ... existing fields ...\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates capacity needed\n    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed\n    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// num_cosets_zc * skip_domain (zerocheck result size)\n    zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed (uses logup_round0_buffer_size from Step 1)\n    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed\n    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// num_cosets_logup * skip_domain (logup result size)\n    logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n}\n```\n\nCompute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926):\n- `local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree`\n- `skip_domain = 1 << l_skip`\n- `num_x = 1 << n_lift` where `n_lift = n.max(0) as usize`\n- `num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1)` (mod.rs:166)\n- `num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg` (mod.rs:213)\n- Zerocheck `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size`\n- Logup `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` (from Step 1)\n- Call `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc, max_temp_bytes)` and the other 5 FFI size functions to get actual sizes.\n\n### Step 4: Compute threshold and pre-allocate\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)\n\nAfter building work items with their buffer sizes:\n\n1. For each of the 6 buffer types, find the maximum across ALL work items.\n2. If the maximum for any buffer type is 0 (e.g., all AIRs have no zerocheck constraints), use capacity 1 as a sentinel (DeviceBuffer panics on size 0). Track this so the fallback path is used for those buffers.\n3. Compute total per-thread bytes from the 6 max values.\n4. Memory budget: `per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)`.\n5. If total per-thread bytes > per_thread_budget: reduce `num_threads` until it fits, same pattern as GKR (gkr_input.rs:296-303).\n6. If after reducing to `num_threads=1` it still exceeds 2GB: skip pre-allocation entirely and use the current dynamic path.\n7. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of `Round0ThreadBuffers`.\n\n### Step 5: Modify evaluation functions to accept pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\n#### D2H copy handling (addresses review finding 1)\n\n`DeviceBuffer` does not distinguish capacity from logical length — `len()` returns the allocation size. `to_host_on_current_stream()` copies `len()` elements. When a pre-allocated buffer has capacity larger than the actual output, the D2H copy would transfer excess data.\n\n**Solution:** Create a correctly-sized `DeviceBuffer` view using `ManuallyDrop` for D2H copies:\n\n```rust\nuse std::mem::ManuallyDrop;\n\n/// Create a non-owning DeviceBuffer view with the correct logical length for D2H copies.\n/// SAFETY: `buf` must have capacity >= `len`, and the caller must ensure `buf` outlives the view.\nunsafe fn device_view<T>(buf: &DeviceBuffer<T>, len: usize) -> ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer<T>> {\n    ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(buf.as_mut_ptr(), len))\n}\n```\n\nThis creates a `DeviceBuffer` that points to the same GPU memory but has the correct `len` for D2H copies. `ManuallyDrop` prevents the Drop impl from freeing the pre-allocated memory.\n\n#### `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` changes\n\nAdd parameter:\n```rust\nprealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>,\n// (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals)\n```\n\nReplace allocation of `intermediates` (lines 63-68):\n```rust\nlet (mut intermediates, owns_intermediates) = if let Some((ref mut pre_inter, _, _)) = prealloc {\n    if intermed_capacity > 0 && pre_inter.len() >= intermed_capacity {\n        // Reuse pre-allocated buffer (no mutex, no alloc)\n        // SAFETY: pre_inter has capacity >= intermed_capacity\n        (unsafe { ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(pre_inter.as_mut_ptr(), intermed_capacity)) }, false)\n    } else {\n        (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity.max(1))), true)\n    }\n} else if intermed_capacity > 0 {\n    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)), true)\n} else {\n    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::new()), false)\n};\n```\n\nApply the same pattern for `temp_sums_buffer` and `sp_evals`.\n\nFor the D2H copy of `sp_evals` in the caller (`process_air_round0`, mod.rs:184):\n```rust\nlet actual_len = w.zc_sp_evals_cap;\nlet view = unsafe { device_view(&bufs.zc_sp_evals, actual_len) };\nlet q_evals = view.to_host_on_current_stream()?;\n```\n\nAt function end: if `owns_intermediates`, explicitly drop (frees via mutex). If not, ManuallyDrop prevents freeing.\n\n#### `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` changes\n\nSame pattern. Add `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).\n\nItems 4-6 (`d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`) remain dynamically allocated. These 3 alloc+free pairs per logup call still go through the mutex. This is unavoidable since their data is AIR-specific and runtime-dependent.\n\n### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nChange signature:\n```rust\nfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n    bufs: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError>\n```\n\nInside the function:\n1. Check if zerocheck buffers fit:\n   ```rust\n   let zc_prealloc = if w.zc_intermed_cap <= bufs.zc_intermediates.len()\n       && w.zc_temp_sums_cap <= bufs.zc_temp_sums.len()\n       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap <= bufs.zc_sp_evals.len()\n       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap > 0\n   {\n       Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))\n   } else {\n       None\n   };\n   ```\n2. Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(..., zc_prealloc)`.\n3. For the D2H copy: if pre-allocated was used, create a `device_view` with the actual output length (`w.zc_sp_evals_cap`). If dynamic allocation was used, the buffer already has the correct length.\n4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()`, the host data is in a `Vec<EF>`. The pre-allocated GPU buffer is safe to reuse for the next AIR.\n5. Same pattern for logup buffers, using `bufs.logup_*`.\n\n### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (Phase 2, lines 963-985)\n\nPass one `Round0ThreadBuffers` to each spawned thread:\n```rust\nlet handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n    .into_iter()\n    .zip(thread_items.into_iter())\n    .enumerate()\n    .map(|(thread_id, (mut bufs, indices))| {\n        let items = &work_items;\n        s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n            let t0 = std::time::Instant::now();\n            let results: Vec<_> = indices\n                .iter()\n                .map(|&idx| process_air_round0(&items[idx], &mut bufs))\n                .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n            tracing::debug!(thread_id, elapsed_ms = t0.elapsed().as_millis(), num_airs = indices.len(), \"round0 thread done\");\n            Ok(results)\n        })\n    })\n    .collect();\n```\n\nFor the single-thread path (`num_threads <= 1`), pass the single buffer set similarly.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.\n2. **D2H copy correctness**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) use `ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(ptr, actual_len)>` views for D2H copies, ensuring exactly the correct number of elements are transferred to host. No excess data is copied.\n3. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function calls `current_stream_sync()` (copy.rs:147), ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete before reuse.\n4. **ManuallyDrop safety**: Views created via `ManuallyDrop` never free GPU memory. Only the owning `Round0ThreadBuffers` (dropped after all threads complete) frees the pre-allocated memory.\n5. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively.\n6. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. If it still exceeds after `num_threads=1`, pre-allocation is skipped entirely.\n7. **APC 0 behavior**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`. If the single AIR's buffers exceed pre-allocated capacity, the fallback path is used.\n8. **Kernel buffer semantics**: Intermediates and temp_sums are scratch space — kernels write to them but the data is never read back to host. Using a pre-allocated buffer with capacity > required is harmless; the kernel indexes only up to `intermed_capacity`, not the buffer's allocated length.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n### Commands\n```bash\n# In powdr repo:\ncd results/pairing\nPROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n\n# Build\ncargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n\n# Before measurements (3 runs for APC 300)\nfor i in 1 2 3; do\n  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion\ndone\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n\n# After implementing the optimization, rebuild and re-measure:\nfor i in 1 2 3; do\n  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion\ndone\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n\npython3 ~/spec.py after_apc300_1/metrics.json after_apc300\n```\n\n### Expected results\n- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-240ms (13-28% improvement)\n- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1385ms (3-5% improvement)\n- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs)\n- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise\n\n### Stability verification\nCompare medians of 3 before-runs vs 3 after-runs for APC 300 to confirm improvement exceeds noise (~20ms).\n\n### Nsight validation\nRun nsight on APC 300 and verify:\n- Fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync API calls in the Round 0 NVTX span\n- Reduced mutex contention visible in CPU thread timeline (fewer blocked intervals)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs). Below the noise floor.\n2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms**. Any single-phase regression (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) > 30ms.\n3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. Fallback path must not add overhead.\n4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed).\n","numLines":335,"startLine":1,"totalLines":335}}}
