{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XZWnogmCQAwAHKJWuXLuyb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the problem clearly:\n\nFor APC 300 segments (n=306 and n=317):\n- max_zc_intermed: 48,234,496 (~48M elements × 4 bytes = 193 MB)\n- p95 zc_intermed: 786,432 (~786K elements × 4 bytes = 3.15 MB)\n- max_logup_intermed: 72,351,744 (~72M elements × 4 bytes = 289 MB)\n\n\n- p95 logup_intermed: 2,629,632 (~2.6M elements × 4 bytes = 10.5 MB)\n\nThe peak memory usage hits ~482 MB per thread, forcing the budget check to throttle from 8 threads down to 2, but the 95th percentile is only ~13.6 MB—nearly 370x smaller. I should switch to using a percentile-based allocation strategy instead of the maximum, letting the rare outliers fall back to dynamic allocation while keeping the common case efficient.\n\nNow I'm updating the code to apply the 95th percentile for pre-allocated buffer sizing...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1312,"cache_read_input_tokens":120961,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1312},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7b52780-6e9b-4892-943d-0d0679c1a1bd","uuid":"dc5ff2d1-0908-471b-80ea-9eff68b8ebd1"}
